# Two-PC sync through GitHub

The researcher runs this project on a desktop PC and a laptop and wants both to
show exactly the same data. GitHub (`tabianayaz/research-valo`, must be
PRIVATE) is the sync channel; the researcher uses GitHub Desktop.

- Everything in `data/` is committed: `app.db`, `backups/`, `exports/`,
  `logs/`, `raw/`, `scraper_settings.json`. Only SQLite temp files
  (`*.db-wal`, `*.db-shm`, `*.db-journal`) are ignored.
- Never re-add a rule that ignores `data/` or `app/data/`. Ignore patterns for
  the data folder must be anchored (`/data/...`), because an unanchored
  `data/` also hides the code package `app/data/`.
- Never delete, reset or regenerate `data/app.db`; it is the shared research
  database.
- Any new runtime file that the app needs to look identical on both PCs must
  live under `data/` (or be committed) — not in a machine-specific location.
- `app.db` is binary and cannot be merged. Remind the researcher of the
  workflow when relevant: Pull before using the app; close the app, commit
  and push after using it; use only one PC at a time.
- Never push research data while the repository is public.
- Commit/push only when the researcher asks.
